WEBVTT

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.230
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:15.570
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.500
The Kuchiba City
Pokémon Eating Contest!

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.500
Once again, proud eaters
have gathered here from all over!

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.880
Standing in the way of the new faces
that are brimming with confidence...

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:36.640
...are last year’s champ, Kabigon,
and our regular eating fighters!

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.020
And this time we have a special guest,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.760
the globe-trotting legend
of the eating world!

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.790
Kaiser Burshamo has
come back to this contest!

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.780
Burshamo!

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.590
Whoever comes out victorious
will receive a free trip to Isshu, plus...

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.910
All-you-can-eat
gourmet Isshu food!

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:00.910
Everyone! Are you ready?!

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.880
It seems Satoshi and Go are taking part
in the Pokémon Eating Contest.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.010
The reason behind this can be traced back
to several days earlier.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:12.830
Everyone!

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.500
Here’s your food!

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.690
They’re asleep...

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.300
Let’s just let them sleep.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.730
Wait, you already finished?!

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:36.630
Want, want!
Hoshii, Hoshii!

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.660
You want more?

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.750
Does your appetite ever end?

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.990
Would you like to
put it to the test?

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.420
The Pokémon Eating Contest?

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.250
That sounds fun!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.820
All right! I’ll win it for sure!

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.170
How naïve.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:59.260
Kuchiba City’s Eating Contest is famous
for attracting veteran eaters.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.180
And that’s not all.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:06.270
This time, the eating world’s top monarch,
Kaiser Burshamo will be attending!

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.520
That sounds fun.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.350
Huh?

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:13.750
I’ll see just how far I can get
with Hoshigarisu!

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.530
Me, too!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.980
Do your best, okay, Kairyu?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.760
I’m counting on you,
Hoshigarisu!

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.660
No way.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.010
They’re entering too?!

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.910
It doesn’t matter.
Focus on the contest for now.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:33.290
We’ve been enduring
days and days of fasting with Morpeko,

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.750
all to build up to this day, meow!

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.010
And because of it, right now,

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.810
Morpeko’s appetite and determination
are bigger than ever before!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:50.560
We just have to let it eat,
and victory will be ours, for sure!

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.540
Then we can enjoy
Isshu’s gourmet food, meow!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.210
The first round is the
Everyone’s Favorite Berries Battle!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:46.720
The top ten contestants who eat the most
berry platters will make it through!

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.360
I really get to see
Kaiser Burshamo eat live!

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.470
I’m so emotional!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.320
I never knew you were
a competitive eating maniac, Kikuna.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.480
Is it really that interesting?

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.570
The best teacher is experience!

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.820
You’ll love it too
once you see it, Koharu!

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.070
Now then, the first round...
starts now!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.780
Whoa! They all leapt on those berries
in perfect unison!

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.290
New competitor Sazandra
digs in beautifully with its three heads!

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:19.500
Another new competitor, Kirikizan,
is strategically slicing the berries to eat them all at once?!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.730
Whoa!

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.300
You can really see
each Pokémon’s unique skills.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.130
Now, as for the regulars
facing them!

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:30.260
Of course, a show of eating
like you’ve come to expect!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.930
Amazing!

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.650
And of course,
<i>this</i> Pokémon is on a whole other level!

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.690
A marvelous combination of
elegance and gluttony!

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.240
That gallant stature...
It truly is the Kaiser!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.770
What will we get to see from its long-awaited
return to the Kuchiba City contest?

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.910
Burshamo! Go for it!

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.790
What’s this?! Sazandra’s momentum
has come to a halt?!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:01.840
You can eat more!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.930
Even if it has three heads,
it only has one stomach, meow!

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.220
It just filled itself up three times as fast!

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:14.500
Oh my! Kirikizan’s hand slipped and
it sliced straight through the plate and the table!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.430
Unfortunately, it’s disqualified!

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.420
They got too excited
and messed up!

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.170
Things like this happen every year!

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.480
I see...

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.150
Now then, how are the
little rookies doing?!

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.490
What is it, Koharu?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.840
They look so slow
compared to the larger Pokémon.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.250
It’s like they’re eating
more delicately, or something...

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.000
Good job spotting that!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.960
That’s because they’re
avoiding the seeds!

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:47.950
Smaller Pokémon will fill up quickly
if they eat the berries whole.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:51.010
So even if it’s a hassle,
they have to leave the seeds.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:54.130
By the rules,
leaving the seeds is allowed!

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:56.790
But you lose precious time
by doing so!

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:00.650
Will the little Pokémon be
dropping out here, as always?!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.020
No, they can’t be fully ruled out...

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.780
Morpeko!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.330
That expression...
How deep is its anger?!

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:13.280
It’s relentlessly
gobbling the berries whole!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.090
Here’s your dish!

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.790
Is this the birth of a new star?!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.290
Go, go, Morpeko!

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:24.950
Oh, and here’s another little one
with a fierce appetite!

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:27.240
It’s Hoshigarisu!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.170
Go ahead and eat all you want!

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.680
Wow!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.650
That’s our Hoshigarisu, all right!

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:34.550
But...

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:39.430
Is it gonna be okay, with that belly?

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.980
It’s about time, Hoshigarisu.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.310
Seed Machine Gun into the air!

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.270
How well-researched!

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.700
It’s splitting the seeds and the fruit
with the lowest possible time loss!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.320
Ah! Good work, Go!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.660
You can do that?!

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.040
We’ll use Seed Machine Gun, too!

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.710
I never taught it that!

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.160
And stop!

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.040
Hold it for now!

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.840
There’s still more to come, meow!

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.340
Hoshigarisu was really strong!

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.390
Just according to plan, yeah?

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.300
How’d you do?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.730
About that...

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:16.970
Kairyu...

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.970
...is a surprisingly light eater.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.570
The results are in!

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.890
Proceeding to the next round...

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.540
...will be these Pokémon!

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.060
All right!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.910
You two really worked hard!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:37.410
Time to cheer on Go with all of you.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.370
Let’s keep going just like that!

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:50.860
You’re excited just about getting here?
I can <i>tell</i> that you’re an amateur.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:53.400
Were you talking to me?

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.600
Everyone here save
Hoshigarisu and that Morpeko...

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.890
...is a title holder from
a large regional contest.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.770
In other words, we’re the pros!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.270
To put it bluntly,
you’ll fade away next round.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.370
What did you say?!

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:07.730
You’ll fade away!

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.980
Oh my,
fight you must not!

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.890
Eat a nice sweet snack, and relax, yes?

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.360
Here you go!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.930
Cookies on the house, meow!

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:19.950
When there’s
another round to come?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.910
There is no problem!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.860
Since everybody here
are the world’s top gluttons!

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.090
Enough that they can’t relax
if they’re not eating, meow!

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.170
Exactly!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.330
Kuitaran was just <i>dying</i> for
something to chew on!

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.090
Same for my Berolinga!

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.930
I was just thinking
we could do with something.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.970
I’ll take it with thanks!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.650
You like it?

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.230
What? Really?

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.610
As I thought.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.680
They’re showing off that
they have room to spare,

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.780
to try and put pressure
on their opponents, meow.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.250
But they don’t know that
it’ll work against them.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.070
Wha— Hey! Morpeko, no!

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.830
Hoshigarisu!
You just went and ate them?!

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.790
Well, the plan went off
without a hitch... somehow.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.720
Those were special cookies
that will swell up in their bellies!

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.490
Hey!

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:27.760
Marunomu!

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.730
My Berolinga!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.230
Don’t worry. It just overate.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.010
From those cookies earlier?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.060
I knew it!

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:42.020
Huh?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.830
Thank you for waiting!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.210
These are the Pokémon who
will face the second round!

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.950
Hmm? Shouldn’t there be more?

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:54.960
Actually, due to an accident,

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:59.960
Yarukimono, Berolinga, Kuitaran and Marunomu
were forced to withdraw.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:01.550
<i>What?</i>

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.300
What happened?

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:07.260
However! The remaining line-up
is full of veteran eaters!

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:08.980
Don’t take your eyes off them yet!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:11.310
They really do look strong!

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.610
Go’s going to have a hard time
whoever he faces!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:16.980
A perfect success.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:19.910
Now, let’s rig a bit more.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.380
The second round will be conducted
in paired battles!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:45.250
The winner of each
will advance to the finals!

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:48.770
Whoever draws the same color of ball
from the lottery will be battling.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.950
What an ironic twist of fate!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.570
Kaiser Burshamo and Champ Kabigon
will be facing off here!

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.570
What?!
But it’s only the second round!

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:09.380
Does that mean the two favorites
are facing one another?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:13.210
That’s not all.
Those two have history between them.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:17.770
It’s a well-known fact that Burshamo
made its Eating Contest debut here,

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:21.010
but in that contest,
Kabigon fought it all the way to the bitter end!

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:23.980
You really do know a lot.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:28.830
Driven by its frustration,
Kabigon entered lots of different contests,

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.980
training itself for the day
when it could face Burshamo again!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:40.190
If the two favorites face off...

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.700
Then even the winner’s
not getting off lightly.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.930
The contestants
have taken their seats!

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:49.410
The first table is...
Burshamo versus Kabigon!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.830
Burshamo!

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:57.150
The second table is
Morpeko versus Onigori!

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.340
Can we hurry up and get going?

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:02.820
The third table,
Hoshigarisu versus Betobeton!

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.220
So <i>you’re</i> my opponent.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.090
I’ll say a requiem for your hopes.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.470
Whoever drew the ball with a symbol
on it in the lottery...

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.540
...gets to choose the menu!

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:13.730
Curry.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.720
Berry pot-au-feu!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.600
Momon tart!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.570
Well then, the second round...
starts now!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.340
The first table is a curry battle!

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:28.570
Both sides have begun eating
with amazing momentum!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:32.330
Burshamo’s so pretty
when it eats, isn’t it?!

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.600
Both of these Pokémon are
previous winners of this contest!

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.330
They’re downing the dishes
with the dignity of monarchs!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:42.900
And, the second table is a piping hot
berry pot-au-feu showdown!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.230
Anger that burns hotter
than pot-au-feu!

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.140
Morpeko doesn’t mind the heat at all!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.100
How about its opponent, Onigori?

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.490
You thought Ice types
don’t like the heat?

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:59.520
Well, my Onigori can
freeze anything and eat it up!

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.090
Onigori, Freeze-Dry!

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.360
You fell for it.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.530
How will you eat it
if you freeze it inside the pot?!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.030
No!

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:15.040
Oh, no! Onigori can’t
eat the berries like this!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.220
A regrettable mistake!

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:21.170
By the way, the rules say you have to finish a dish
before requesting the next one!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.920
Eat as much as you want!

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.120
Here comes more servings!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.750
The third table is
a Momon tart battle!

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:31.230
Hoshigarisu looks like
it’s enjoying it,

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:33.680
but Betobeton looks like
it’s struggling!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.540
That Betobeton
doesn’t like sweet food, right?

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.310
I realized it earlier.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:44.820
You came over to pick a fight,
but you left the moment the cookies showed up.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:49.570
Because you didn’t want to ruin Betobeton’s appetite
with food it doesn’t like, right?

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:54.070
Even if that was the case,
you’re still going to lose.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:54.830
What?

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.550
We’re pros.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:00.330
We’ve trained and trained so that Betobeton’s
able to stomach any food, even if it hates it.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.630
But how about Hoshigarisu?

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.840
No matter how much you like a food,
eat it too much and you get sick of it!

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:10.020
What’s this?!
Hoshigarisu’s paws have stopped!

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:11.340
This isn’t good!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.440
Go!

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:15.810
Competitive eating
challenges your endurance, too!

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.520
Keep at it!

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.270
I expected that, yeah?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.970
Hoshigarisu, the taste changer!

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:29.610
The trainer commanded Hoshigarisu to
pour Matoma berry juice over the tart?!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.070
What?!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.950
Great work, Go!

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.830
You reset the sweet taste in its mouth
with the fierce taste of Matoma!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.590
I-I knew you could do it, Go!

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:48.120
Hoshigarisu is
refreshed and recovered!

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:51.400
By the way,
bringing in spices is allowed!

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:56.100
Each table is in the last spurt!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.730
And stop!

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:14.120
First, the center of attention, the first table.
And as expected, he took the win!

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:16.210
Kaiser Burshamo!

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:20.250
He’s even handsome in victory!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:25.020
The winner at the second table was
the enraged appetite of Morpeko!

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:26.410
We did it!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.850
And the winner of table three was
the eye of the storm here today!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.710
Hoshigarisu!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.890
Natural, yeah?

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.640
You did it!

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.640
Go made it to the finals?

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:42.230
Yay!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.210
We’ve basically won already, meow!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:50.110
Now, the Eating Contest is in its final stage!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:56.370
The last dish is... Kuchiba City’s new delicacy,
bubbly Achamo manju!

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.280
Burshamo, go for it!

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.150
Don’t give up, Hoshigarisu!

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.680
Fight, fight, Morpeko!

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:10.130
Well then, the final... starts now!

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.780
Morpeko’s expression
is as incredible as ever!

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.860
It’s fueling its appetite
with its swirling hatred,

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.390
taking it out on the Achamo manju!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.220
All right, keep it coming!

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:22.220
Go on, go on!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:24.930
Hoshigarisu is
chasing after Morpeko!

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.220
And still with a smile on its face!

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.610
It’s happily enjoying
the Achamo manju!

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:32.110
You’re making good pace,
Hoshigarisu!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.920
The ferocious Morpeko...

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:36.370
Hoshigarisu forging its own path...

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.870
They’re both piling up plates!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.620
How will the monarch,
Kaiser Burshamo take them down?!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:44.750
Huh?

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.920
What happened?!

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.770
It’s not eating...
In fact, it hasn’t taken a single bite!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.440
It’s unbelievable!

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.080
Burshamo...

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:14.350
Burshamo evolves from
Achamo, after all...

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.080
Oh, Kaiser...

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:31.280
Is it protecting the weak chicks?!

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:35.090
An unexpected departure
for Kaiser Burshamo!

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:39.280
But... Even that kind side...
I love it!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.990
The shock is spreading!

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:44.850
The winner is going to be
one of the two newcomers!

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.760
Yay! Looking good!

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:48.320
Now that Burshamo’s out...

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.660
Victory lies in our hands, meow!

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:51.940
No!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.240
The future lies in <i>my</i> hands!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.570
<i>No way!</i>

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:03.670
With a smile like it was never scowling in the first place,
Morpeko stopped eating?!

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:05.850
Hey! You’re nearly there!
Keep going!

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:07.870
What happened to that momentum
from earlier?!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.590
Look, there’s still more manju!

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:11.820
Eat some more!

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:13.960
Eat up, meow!

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.340
Is Morpeko finished eating?!

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.850
Which leaves only Hoshigarisu!

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:26.040
It’s only one plate behind Morpeko!

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.350
If it can break past it,
it’ll be the winner!

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.850
This is our chance!
Dig in and pull ahead!

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.470
That belly...

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:35.610
It looks painful.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.790
Hoshigarisu’s small body...!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:41.110
Just one more plate!
But that plate will not fit!

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:46.860
Hoshigarisu...
Can’t you eat anymore?

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:50.000
But, Hoshigarisu’s eyes
have not given up!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.230
It’s boldly tackling
the Achamo manju!

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:54.960
Why go so far...?

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.200
Because there is food to be eaten!

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.720
That’s the only reason!

00:19:58.720 --> 00:19:59.970
Go for it!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:04.680
You can do it! Go! Hoshigarisu!

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.570
You...

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.570
It evolved!

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:24.570
Yokubarisu’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.480
Yokubarisu!

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:30.150
Yokubarisu! Greedy Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:33.960
It has strong teeth and can
chew through the toughest of berry shells.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.530
What’s this?! A Pokémon has evolved
during the contest!

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:43.300
And that’s not all! It keeps eating with a ferocious momentum,
shooting straight past Morpeko’s record!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:48.240
And now, Hoshigarisu—
no, Yokubarisu’s victory is decided!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:52.590
We did it!

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:54.510
You won it!

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:58.570
I get it, I get it, calm down...

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:00.770
So, Koharu?

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:04.110
I never thought I’d get so invested
in an Eating Contest!

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.320
Right?!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.670
Congrats, Yokubarisu!

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:09.570
Let’s keep working together!

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:17.290
Go and Hoshigarisu achieved a marvelous victory
in the Pokémon Eating Contest.

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:22.210
With their prize,
they’re setting off for Isshu next!

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:29.130
I can’t cope with this, meow.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.580
After all this,
I need some comfort food!

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:34.340
Why?

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:35.440
Don’t tell me...

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.600
It’s already hungry again, meow?

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:40.830
<i>No way!</i>

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:51.600
Mew!

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:52.350
Warrgle!

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:53.140
Runpappa!

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:53.910
Pawou!

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:54.650
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.650 --> 00:21:55.440
Strike!

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:56.240
Cresselia!

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:56.950
Amakaji!

00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:57.760
Jirachi!

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:58.560
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.560 --> 00:21:59.330
Kibago!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:00.100
Gonbe!

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:00.880
Bayleaf!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.380
Freezer!

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:03.570
Zacian!

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:20.420
Mew!

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:21.250
Wooper!

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:21.970
Pachirisu!

00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:22.820
Sunaba!

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:23.480
Absol!

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:24.340
Lunala!

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:25.150
Rabbifoot!

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:25.930
Tropius!

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:26.700
Sunahebi!

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:27.570
Vibrava!

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:28.220
Burshamo!

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:28.990
Mokuroh!

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:29.810
Rotom!

00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:30.530
Mooland!

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:31.310
Dodorio!

00:22:31.310 --> 00:22:32.030
Otosupus!

00:22:32.030 --> 00:22:32.850
Swanna!

00:22:32.850 --> 00:22:33.600
Nazonokusa!

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:34.420
Samehada!

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:35.190
Darkrai!

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:35.870
Iwanko!

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:36.700
Cortoise!

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:37.530
Scorupi!

00:22:37.530 --> 00:22:38.310
Pippi!

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:39.030
Pinpuku!

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:39.810
Kunugidama!

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:40.550
Mankey!

00:22:40.550 --> 00:22:41.360
Kimori!

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:42.180
Ligray!

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:43.610
Rayquaza!

00:22:43.610 --> 00:22:44.340
Zamazenta!

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:09.510
Now, onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:10.740
Go!

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:14.620
The prize from the
Pokémon Eating Contest,

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:18.490
an Isshu all-you-can-eat
gourmet food tour begins!

00:23:18.490 --> 00:23:21.460
Huh? Where’s Aceburn and Lucario?

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:25.960
We don’t intend to lose to
bouncy Pokémon like you!

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:30.850
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:33.700
A Close Call with the Pretty-Much-Pikachu!
